@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Build budget and header checks
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
actor "Developer or CI" as ci
box "Build and deploy tooling" #F2F4F7
  participant "ng build --stats-json" as build
  participant "InitialLoadCheck" as budget
  participant "Static host" as host
  participant "HeaderCheck" as headers
end box

ci -> build : npm run build
build --> budget : dist/ and stats.json (esbuild metafile)
budget -> budget : Initial files + home route chunk + their static imports + global CSS
budget -> budget : gzip each (level 9) and sum
alt Sum ≤ 250 KB (A-08)
  budget --> ci : ok, with the per-file table
else Over budget
  budget --> ci : exit 1 — the build fails (NFR-004)
end
== After each deploy ==
ci -> host : Deploy dist/ with headers from deploy/security-headers.json
ci -> headers : check https://<host>/
headers -> host : GET / and GET /ngsw-worker.js
host --> headers : Response headers
headers -> headers : Compare each with the expected value (NFR-014)
headers --> ci : ok, or the missing or different headers
@enduml
